\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Add:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 --bg
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}Example:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 lexicon data --get example-source --bg
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}The same option may be used with processing:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 lexicon data --process example-source --bg
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Abandon a Previous Failed Session\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Add:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 --abandon-past-fail
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}Example:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 lexicon data --get example-source --abandon-past-fail
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}Options may be combined:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 lexicon data --get example-source --bg --abandon-past-fail
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Source-Specific Arguments\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Lexicon-level arguments appear before 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 --
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 .\
{\listtext	\'95	}Arguments after 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 --
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2  are passed directly to the selected source implementation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Example:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 lexicon data --get example-source --bg -- <source-specific arguments>
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}This allows each source implementation to define its own arguments without adding them to the global Lexicon CLI.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Raw Data Layout\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Raw acquisition data is stored under:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 sources/<source-name>/data/raw/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}Each network transaction receives its own directory:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 data/raw/<request-timestamp>-<id>/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}Each transaction contains:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl1
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}request/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\ls9\ilvl1
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}response/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}request/metadata.json
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2  stores structured request metadata such as:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl1\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}timestamp;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}method;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}URL;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}headers;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}protocol information;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}payload size and hash where applicable.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}request/body
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2  contains the original request-body bytes when a request body exists.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}response/metadata.json
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2  stores structured response metadata such as:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl1\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}timestamp;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}HTTP status;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}headers;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}protocol information;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}payload size and hash.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}response/body
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2  contains the response payload bytes as received.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The raw layer does not interpret a response body as HTML, JSON, ZIP, audio, text, or any other semantic format merely because its content type is known.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Authentication secrets and equivalent credentials must not be persisted unredacted in raw request metadata.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Sessions\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Get-raw-data execution/session state is stored under:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 sources/<source-name>/get-raw-data/sessions/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}Its current session state is tracked in:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 sources/<source-name>/get-raw-data/session_status.json
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}Process-data execution/session state is stored separately under:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 sources/<source-name>/process-data/sessions/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}Its current session state is tracked in:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 sources/<source-name>/process-data/session_status.json
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}Session records describe execution state. They are separate from the raw request/response data stored under 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 data/raw/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Lexicon Core\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Shared behavior lives under:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 core/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}core/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2  is one Rust library crate.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Lexicon Core defines the public contracts that source implementations must satisfy.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Core contains shared get-raw-data behavior, process-data behavior, fa\'e7ade logic, and session-engine machinery.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Internal engine modules are private to the Core crate.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Source implementations may depend on Core\'92s public API but may not directly access private engine implementation types.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Core must not expose concrete private-engine types through its public contracts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Adding a New Source\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Adding or modifying source implementations requires a Rust development toolchain.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Create a source draft with:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 lexicon source <source-name> --draft
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}The command creates the mandatory source structure, including:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl1
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}data/raw/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 ;\
\ls12\ilvl1
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}data/processed/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 ;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}get-raw-data session files;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}process-data session files;\
\ls12\ilvl1
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}get_raw_data_impl/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 ;\
\ls12\ilvl1
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}process_data_impl/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 ;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}their Cargo manifests;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}their Rust source entry points;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}the source-specific 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 processing/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2  directory.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Get-Raw-Data Implementation\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Implement retrieval behavior in:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 sources/<source-name>/get-raw-data/get_raw_data_impl/src/{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://main.rs/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 main.rs}}
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}The generated implementation must satisfy the 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 GetRawData
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2  contract defined by Lexicon Core.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Rust\'92s compiler is responsible for enforcing this contract.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Process-Data Implementation\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls14\ilvl0
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Implement processing behavior in:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 sources/<source-name>/process-data/process_data_impl/src/{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://main.rs/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 main.rs}}
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}The generated implementation must satisfy the 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 ProcessData
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2  contract defined by Lexicon Core.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Source-specific processing files belong under:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 sources/<source-name>/process-data/process_data_impl/processing/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Add and Build a Source\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl0
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}After implementing the source, run:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 lexicon source <source-name> --add
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}Lexicon will:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl1\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}locate the source\'92s implementation Cargo projects;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}compile the implementations against Lexicon Core;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}allow the Rust compiler to verify the required traits;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}reject implementations that do not satisfy their Core contracts;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}link successful implementations into native executables for the current target;\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}place the resulting executables into their respective implementation directories.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Adding a source does not require modifying Lexicon Core or registering the source in a central source list.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Rebuild for the Current Machine\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls16\ilvl0
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}A concrete repository containing multiple source implementations may provide:\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 lexicon build
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
{\listtext	\'95	}This rebuilds all discovered source implementations for the current operating system and CPU architecture.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The command discovers implementations from the mandated source-directory structure rather than from a manually maintained registry.\
{\listtext	\'95	}This allows the same source repository to be cloned on Windows, Linux, or macOS and rebuilt into native executables appropriate for that machine.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Runtime Requirements\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls17\ilvl0
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Normal users do not need Rust, Cargo, Zig, Python, the JVM, or another language runtime to execute already-built Lexicon operations.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Normal commands execute native binaries directly.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Rust/Cargo is required only when creating, changing, validating, or rebuilding Rust source implementations.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Cross-target release builds may use additional build tooling, such as Zig-assisted Rust linking, but that tooling is not required for ordinary runtime use.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 This keeps 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 example-source
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2  as the sole concrete source example while 
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 core/
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2  and the CLI remain completely domain-agnostic.\
}